  "academic": "Reopened the current Dutch OER and internship record before reconsidering the comparison. The single bachelor allocates 60 EC in year one, 69 EC of later core, 39 EC of elective space including at least 6 EC free choice, and 12 EC of individual final research. The Quantum Mechanics 1 current catalogue presumes introductory quantum mechanics and linear algebra; both are in the ordinary first-year curriculum. The dual-degree transition is unnecessary. UCR coursework supplies real wave physics, introductory mechanics, thermodynamics, applied electromagnetic surveys, environmental materials work, and laboratory, mathematics, imaging and data methods. Even a generous combination lacks the progression through mechanics, electromagnetic theory, quantum physics, astronomy and experimental physics. The five withdrawn schedule conflicts do not determine the outcome.",
  "content": "Checked the Physics and Astronomy title and institution, the overview and comparison explanation, curriculum year and route, every component label and credit, all component notes and source URLs. The exception renderer displays the audience explanation, official source and complete Radboud curriculum. No UCR programme, alignment, course description, selected note or UCR link applies.",
